※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ Everything an expression is made of is worked out in the order it is written,
※ left to right.  Nothing in the language shows this except a call, since a call
※ is the only thing that can be noticed happening -- which is exactly why the
※ order has to be stated rather than left to whatever the compiler finds easier.
※
※ `note` records the order it was called in, each call pushing a digit: the
※ digits read left to right are the order the calls were made in.
※
※ The three lists a program can write are all here -- a call's arguments, a
※ tuple's members, an array's elements -- and a tuple handed over as several
※ arguments is worked out where it stands, not before the arguments written to
※ its left.  A binary operator is here too, because precedence does not move
※ anything: `a + b × c` groups the multiplication first and still works `a` out
※ first, the order being the order of the writing and not the shape of the tree.

let order: mut u8 = 0u8

@[impure]
fn note(n: u8) → u8:
    order ← order × 5u8 + n
    n

@[impure]
fn pair_of(n: u8) → 〈u8, u8〉:
    〈note(n), note(n + 1u8)〉

fn four(a: u8, b: u8, c: u8, d: u8) → u8:
    a + b + c + d

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    ※ 1, then the two the spread stands for, then 4
    let sum: u8 = four(note(1u8), ⁂pair_of(2u8), note(4u8))
    let arguments: u8 = order
    order ← 0u8
    ※ the same over a tuple's members
    let made: 〈u8, u8, u8, u8〉 = 〈note(1u8), ⁂pair_of(2u8), note(4u8)〉
    let members: u8 = order
    order ← 0u8
    ※ an array's elements, and an operator whose right side binds tighter
    let v: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦note(1u8), note(2u8)⟧
    let worked: u8 = note(3u8) + v⟦0⟧ × note(4u8)
    let elements: u8 = order
    ※ 1,2,3,4 pushed in turn is ((1×5+2)×5+3)×5+4 = 194
    let counted: u8 = sum + made⟦3⟧ + worked + 21u8
    ※ 10 + 4 + (3 + 1×4) = 21, and what this used to say through the exit
    ※ status, which is six bits now
    if arguments = 194u8 ∧ members = 194u8 ∧ elements = 194u8 ∧ counted = 42u8:
        0u6
    else:
        1u6
